      "title_align": "left",
      "section": "Families and architectures",
      "order": 3,
      "alignment": "left",
      "vertical_alignment": "top",
      "body": "Two profile HMMs, DemoFamA (residues 30 to 101 of the demo protein) and DemoFamB (102 to 172), shown as logos with the domain hits that matched them, the same hits drawn as domain architectures, and the demo protein in 3D. The HMMs are estimated from the demo alignment by the fixture script, not by hmmbuild, and the hits are synthetic: scores follow identity times coverage. Click a state in the logo, a domain or a residue in 3D to select that range in every tile; hover marks it. The other 33 proteins are members of the alignment and have no structure, so only the demo protein follows into 3D; six of them are fragments, whose domains match only part of the model (zigzag edge).\n",
      "surface": "none",
      "accent": null,
      "logo": null,
      "logo_dark": null,
      "wf_tag": "python/advanced_viz_demo"
    },
